#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# log_plot

#% text
# `log_plot(f, [x, a, b])` draws the curve of `f` for `x` from `a` to `b` with a logarithmic y axis.

#% text
# `log_plot([f1, f2, ...], [x, a, b])` draws several curves.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `log_plot` is `plot` with `y_scale: log`, and takes the same options.

#% item
# Values that are not positive have no logarithm and are left out, which breaks the curve.

#% item
# On a logarithmic axis an exponential exp(c x) is a straight line of slope c.

#% item
# The value is `image("path")`, a PNG file.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# The exponential function is a straight line:

#% cell
log_plot(exp(x), [x, 0, 10])
#% output
#= image("log_plot.files/log_plot-1.png")

#% text
# Several curves:

#% cell
log_plot([exp(x), exp(2x), x^2], [x, 0.1, 5])
#% output
#= image("log_plot.files/log_plot-2.png")

#% text
# A Gaussian is a parabola:

#% cell
log_plot(exp(-x^2), [x, -5, 5])
#% output
#= image("log_plot.files/log_plot-3.png")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Values over many orders of magnitude:

#% cell
log_plot(gamma(x), [x, 0.5, 10])
#% output
#= image("log_plot.files/log_plot-4.png")

#% text
# Zeros of the function drop down the axis:

#% cell
log_plot(abs(sin(x)), [x, 0, 10])
#% output
#= image("log_plot.files/log_plot-5.png")

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# Labels and a legend:

#% cell
log_plot([exp(x), exp(-x)], [x, -3, 3], x_label: "x", legend: ["growth", "decay"])
#% output
#= image("log_plot.files/log_plot-6.png")

#% text
# A fixed vertical range:

#% cell
log_plot(exp(x), [x, 0, 10], plot_range: [1, 10^3])
#% output
#= image("log_plot.files/log_plot-7.png")

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# Radioactive decay of two isotopes and their sum; each separate decay is a straight line:

#% cell
log_plot([exp(-t), 0.5*exp(-t/5), exp(-t) + 0.5*exp(-t/5)], [t, 0, 15], x_label: "t", legend: ["fast", "slow", "total"])
#% output
#= image("log_plot.files/log_plot-8.png")

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The same plot as `plot` with a logarithmic y axis:

#% cell
plot(exp(x), [x, 0, 10], y_scale: log)
#% output
#= image("log_plot.files/log_plot-9.png")

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# Where the function is negative nothing is drawn:

#% cell
log_plot(x^2 - 1, [x, -2, 2])
#% output
#= image("log_plot.files/log_plot-10.png")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `plot`, `log_log_plot`, `log_linear_plot`, `list_log_plot`, `y_scale`
